## Goal
Visualize overall sample relationships through principal component analysis (PCA) of gene expression counts. Generate a biplot showing samples in PC space, colored by treatment status (treated vs untreated) to assess treatment effect and sample clustering patterns.

## Inputs
Artifact types resolve through each sub-stage's OUTPUTS.tsv at execution time; the paths
below are what they resolve to today.

| Artifact type | Resolved from | Path |
|---|---|---|
| counts_gene | rnaseq_bulk/01_nfcore-rnaseq-wrapper | 02_bioinformatics/rnaseq_bulk/01_nfcore-rnaseq-wrapper/run/results/star_salmon/salmon.merged.gene_counts_length_scaled.tsv |

## Method
1. Load gene counts matrix from the resolved counts_gene artifact (TSV format).
2. Filter genes: retain only genes with mean count ≥ 1 across all samples to reduce noise.
3. Normalize counts using log2(count + 1) transformation to stabilize variance.
4. Perform PCA on the normalized gene-by-sample matrix using scikit-learn (n_components=2).
5. Load sample metadata from the project's samples.csv to extract condition labels (treated vs untreated).
6. Generate a scatter plot in matplotlib showing PC1 vs PC2, with points colored by condition (red for treated, blue for untreated). Add sample labels, explained variance annotations on axes, and a legend.
7. Save the plot as a high-resolution PNG (300 dpi) to results/pca_plot.png.
8. Write a brief summary table (results/pca_summary.csv) listing each sample, its condition, PC1 and PC2 coordinates, and total variance explained by the first two PCs.
All steps run in the gars-bio conda environment.

